From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oasis <oasis@localhost>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:57:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] clamp samp_frac_num instead of returning
 RESAMPLER_ERR_OVERFLOW

UXP follow-up refinement absent from update.sh: when the recomputation
in speex_resampler_set_rate_frac would overflow, clamp samp_frac_num to
den_rate-1 rather than returning the then-new error code. Applied
verbatim so the tree matches the pinned UXP sources byte-for-byte.
---
diff --git a/libspeexdsp/resample.c b/libspeexdsp/resample.c
index d99595a..7c6ef12 100644
--- a/libspeexdsp/resample.c
+++ b/libspeexdsp/resample.c
@@ -1151,7 +1151,9 @@ EXPORT int speex_resampler_set_rate_frac(SpeexResamplerState *st, spx_uint32_t r
       for (i=0;i<st->nb_channels;i++)
       {
          if (!_muldiv_safe(st->samp_frac_num[i],st->den_rate,old_den))
-            return RESAMPLER_ERR_OVERFLOW;
+         {
+             st->samp_frac_num[i] = st->den_rate-1;
+         }
          st->samp_frac_num[i]= _muldiv(st->samp_frac_num[i],st->den_rate,old_den);
          /* Safety net */
          if (st->samp_frac_num[i] >= st->den_rate)
